everage giant  claiming that the trucks will be used at  two different facilities in California  the semi features a tri-motor Powertrain  that produces instant torque and  unparalleled power at any speed allowing  drivers to merge safely while keeping up  with traffic also according to Tesla  charging with electricity is  approximately 2.5 times cheaper per mile  than refueling with diesel do you know  what that means for the company they'll  save up to 200 000 US Dollars within the  first three years not only that but the  semi will also minimize downtime because  it can charge up to 70 percent in as  little as 30 minutes the fans have also  noticed Tesla updating their semi-press  Gallery which means the release is  definitely happening even though there  have been a lot of changes from the  version Elon showed us in 2017 you can  still recognize the semi-truck from a  mile away the massive mirrors and a  slightly revised Greenhouse are the most  distinctive features along with new door  handles black trim at the back of the  cab and exposed rear wheels as for the  interior of the semi truck it's evident  the engineers went the extra mile to  make it unique and exciting it's been  revamped to appear more production ready  with a new console and a steering wheel  featuring controls a few modifications  have been made to the original dashboard  too and the new version seems to have a  tiered design now I must remind you here  that fans initially hesitated to believe  the semi truck was actually happening  because of the delay we've seen in its  launch nevertheless I'm hopeful we'll  get to see the actual vehicle this time  and Elon wasn't just trolling with his  tweet next up let us dive a little  deeper into the features that make the  new Tesla semi unlike any other vehicle  on the market features and pricing Tesla  says the semi will offer approximately  300 and 500 Mile ranges with active  safety features that ensure traction and  stability in all conditions an